      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that sleep recovery is when sleep “rebounds to make up for what was missed.” The packet uses terms like “compensatory sleep” and “augmented” NREM/REM during recovery, but it does not explicitly support the specific phrasing/claim that it is “making up for what was missed.”",
        "The remainder of the definition (compensatory/recovery after sleep loss/forced awakening; after REM sleep deprivation there is a rebound of REM sleep, with NREM sometimes also involved) is broadly supported by the packet, but the unsupported “make up for what was missed” element prevents a pass."
